<title>NIGERIA: Nigeria's weekly forex demand tumbles to $47.4 mln.</title>
<headline>Nigeria's weekly forex demand tumbles to $47.4 mln.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria's central bank said on Friday it sold $47.4 million at a rate of 85 to the dollar at its weekly auction this week.</p>
<p>Last week the bank sold $77.36 million at the rate of 85 naira to the dollar.</p>
<p>Dealers said demand dropped after the central bank asked banks to provide details of forex end-users in order to stem capital flight and speculative buying.</p>
<p>($1=85)</p>
<p>--Lagos newsroom +234 1 263 03 17</p>
